From 3d43256a37cced9750a720f76b1908ebd954d506 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 18:13:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03135/11362] [outer-loop] fix the gate to the REAL per-level
 efficiency metric + ship early-stop (off)

TWO fixes from the per-level-metric finding (operator: 'both'):

(B) GATE METRIC CORRECTION (the load-bearing one). The local gate measured median
TOTAL actions, but the real ARC-AGI-3 score is PER-LEVEL: sum over solved levels of
min(human_actions/agent_actions_for_level, 1)^2 (requirements doc 2026-06-17). The
old whole-game formula scored an efficient-but-over-running solve at ~0 -- lp85
solves L1 in 20 actions (human=17) but ran to 7792 hunting unreachable deeper
levels, so the old metric said 0. We (and .417/.418) were optimizing the WRONG
number.
  - arc_leaderboard_eval.run_game: track per-level action deltas; efficiency is now
    sum min(human[level]/agent_actions_for_level,1)^2. Verified live: lp85 eff=0.7225
    (was ~0). Emits eff= on the result line + a per_level breakdown.
  - arc_local_submission_gate: PRIMARY verdict metric is now CORE per-level
    efficiency (higher=better); median-actions demoted to a wall-clock fallback used
    only when efficiency data is absent (so B2's fixtures + an un-re-baselined gate
    keep working). CORE solve-set containment unchanged. 5 new fixtures + B2's 12 all
    green (17 passed).

(A) EARLY-STOP mechanism (StepwiseExplorer, OFF by default -> live config unchanged).
Smart grace-period: stop K moves after the LAST level-up if no new level, WITHOUT
capping levels (consecutive level-ups reset the window). Under the per-level metric
this is a WALL-CLOCK lever (frees compute budget for more games), NOT a score lever
-- the over-run does not hurt a solved level's score. 5 unit tests. SUBMITTED_EARLY_
STOP_GRACE=None until a K is operator-approved.

NOTE: arc_competition_agent.py also carries the conductor's in-flight .418 A1
batch-expand constants (committed forward per commit-first; A1 continues from here).
Re-baseline (--update-baseline) needed to persist efficiency into the baseline and
activate the primary metric (next step).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
